# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (see com.hakios.demo.plist).
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn started by launchd
/redwood/bin/svc_test
/redwood/bin/surf_test
/bin/ps -A
/redwood/bin/mg_test
# the processors: how many, and -- once the system has settled -- whether they work at the same time
/redwood/bin/cpu_test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 240 &
# and one thing more than the tests: a hand that is not a finger. Ninety seconds in, press home
# through /dev/hakios-touch (rwtouch, src/rwtouch.c): if the ring, the node, the virtual HID in
# backboardd, and SpringBoard all answer, the screen visibly goes home. This is the input path
# proven without waiting for anyone's finger -- and it is what the operator can see for certain.
# on the desktop a home press is invisible -- what is visible from anywhere is the notification
# center: a drag down from the top edge. If the input path works, a panel slides down around
# the ninetieth second, and slides away again when touched.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 90 swipe 0.5 0.01 0.5 0.6 400
